{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1504197-newb-help-atavisms-that-do-direct-damage","id":1504197,"title":"Newb Help - Atavisms that do direct damage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-02T06:06:07-08:00","id":1504197,"title":"Newb Help - Atavisms that do direct damage","content":"Cyclopean Strength, Titanic Blow, Crushing Coils<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Do any of these do these Atavisms do direct damage? They all seem to reference objects and durability. But what if I used Crushing Coils on a mortal's body? What if I used Titanic Blow on someone's head? What about with Cyclopean Strength only effects lifting and throwing? I can't use that strength for other purposes?<br /> <br /> <br /> Thank you in advance!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27665-variable","name":"Variable","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27665_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T10:18:23-08:00","id":1504213,"title":"","content":"What exactly do you mean by &quot;direct damage?&quot; In general though powers do what they say they do. Many powers (not just in Beast) only apply to a subset of actions as broad boosts can have a lot of unintended interactions. For example there was a Changeling: the Lost 1e power that activated with a Strength roll... that boosted your Strength. In the right situations you could get game breaking high Strength for along no real cost because there wasn't wording to keep the power from making activating it again even better (even if your ST ruled each activation didn't stack, your pool would keep getting bigger so you'd keep getting better activation rolls for better results).<br /> <br /> As such, a power like Titanic Blow is about destroying objects, not directly hurting people. Using it on someones head is pointless because that's not what it's for... unless you want to shatter a helmet they're wearing or some other thing of that nature because it would matter.<br /> <br /> Cyclopean Strength -<br /> <br /> Normal only affects Feats on Strength and isn't going to impact damage directly. You can become strong enough to throw a car off a cliff, but the damage will be determined by the falling/crash rules, not your stats after that point.<br /> <br /> Low Satiety's effect can increase your thrown or melee damage output if you're using improvised weapons.<br /> <br /> Expenditure may or may not count as &quot;direct&quot; damage, but that bonus applies to Strength rolls to close combat attacks and grapple, which is going to massively increase your damage per hit. Automatic successes in CofD 2e rules are insanely potent because one success is always enough to succeed in most actions. Even at Lair 1, if you use this, anyone that doesn't use the Dodge combat move is going to get hit by your Strength based attacks whatever your dice turn up. Coupled with the Low Satiety bonus and you're going to be clobbering anything near you into mush if you can find a good improvised weapon.<br /> <br /> Titanic Blow -<br /> <br /> Normal and Low Satiety don't cause any direct damage, though as noted in the text, Low Satiety's effect can indirectly harm people akin to using Cyclopean Strength to toss a car full of people off a cliff.<br /> <br /> Expenditure does deal 1B damage to anyone that fails the save against it. Though again, it also has a lot of potential indirect damage applications.<br /> <br /> Crushing Coils -<br /> <br /> Normal is again, not providing immediate damage, but as a grapple booster it is going to improve your grapple damage output (esp. since lots of things can't escape you and would have to try to out wrestle you instead). As your Lair grows and this bonus starts to increase your Exceptional Success rates for starting grapples, remember that means you can initiate a group and hurt someone in the same turn.<br /> <br /> Low Satiety is a largely protective power that makes sure you're insane grip doesn't get you killed.<br /> <br /> Expenditure is another indirect power. As noted n the text you can't target a living being with it. But you can target an object living being are in and crush them if they can't escape in time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T13:20:31-08:00","id":1504222,"title":"","content":"May I advise creating a single thread for all your questions.<br /> <br /> Anyways, I assume you're asking about Atavisms that do direct damage in the same way a wizard might do direct damage with Fireball, Lightning Bolt, or Cone of Frost in DnD. Off the top of my head, Dragonfire, Smashing Currents, and I think the Low Satiety tier of Storm-Lashed let you jsut target someone like that, but the overall design sense of Beast leans away from doing stuff like that-Astral shamanoids they may be, but they are first mythic monsters who lean into physicality and the way the soul deep anxieites would be made manifest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T17:26:27-08:00","id":1504232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1504197-newb-help-atavisms-that-do-direct-damage?p=1504213#post1504213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Automatic successes in CofD 2e rules are insanely potent because one success is always enough to succeed in most actions. Even at Lair 1, if you use this, anyone that doesn't use the Dodge combat move is going to get hit by your Strength based attacks whatever your dice turn up.</div> </div> </div> </div>My general interpretation has been that by &quot;automatic successes,&quot; Cyclopean Strength is referring to the Extra Successes permutation most commonly encountered as the bonus damage from attacks with weapons, i.e. you add your Lair rating in successes to a successful roll, rather than scarcely needing to roll at all to attain basic success.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T18:25:19-08:00","id":1504236,"title":"","content":"That is a fair interpretation, and is still extremely potent (I mean, if you're someone trying to get the most out of Cyclopean Strength you're going to success most rolls and get to add the successes anyway), but the wording is different from the Extra Successes one... so it would be valid to go either way. A lot of Atavisms skip rolling on only roll because how many successes still matters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}